{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>To shedim.</b> Like \"to se'irim,\" which they whore after; therefore R. Isaac ben Saul [of blessed memory] explained לא שערום אבותיכם — your fathers did not fear them — as derived from לשעירים. According to the one who says: לשדים draws itself and another with it. And so it is: shedim and no elohah. In my opinion there is no need, only its meaning is: to shedim that are not elohim, and they were called shedim on the pattern of אמים from שוד הדעת:" "<b>Elohim they did not know.</b> And how did they think they were elohim and not know this by proof? And this word ידעום is not by transposition, and this is לא שערום אבותיכם:" "<b>New ones, recently they came.</b> From a few days ago; they are not ancient — even your fathers did not know them:" "<b>שערום.</b> Meaning, they did not fear them. Derived from וישער עליו, like the meaning of תסמר שערת בשרי, and it is close to the derivation of סערה. And if it is with samekh, it is like בני יצאוני — they went out from me — חזקתני — you strengthened me — and חזקת from me [is possible]. And behold, its meaning is: and they did not fear them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:00.503007861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}